file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: break_continue
timeout: 30
why: AP 6.7.5.10 NOTE 1 terminates the closest-containing repetitive-statement and no other. Not putting the enclosing loop's targets back after a body leaves an inner loop's blocks in scope for the outer one, so an outer break written after an inner loop has finished branches into the middle of the outer body and the program does not terminate. This is the mutant that found the case: every nested test in the corpus broke the *inner* loop, which a defect this shape answers correctly.
